00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:04,935
A.

2
00:00:04,935 --> 00:00:13,180
Amy is learning about the craft of tie-dying and has found an article about it.

3
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:18,480
Read the article and answer the questions below.

4
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:22,655
Do you have a tie-dyed t-shirt?

5
00:00:22,655 --> 00:00:33,910
Tie-dying is an old art with a history of over 1,500 years and it became most popular in the Tang dynasty.

6
00:00:33,910 --> 00:00:36,825
Here are the steps for tie-dying.

7
00:00:36,825 --> 00:00:41,350
First, twist a piece of cloth and tie it with string.

8
00:00:41,350 --> 00:00:46,540
Then dye the material and when it is dry untie it.

9
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:52,735
The tied part stays the same colour as before but the rest has a different colour.

10
00:00:52,735 --> 00:01:05,050
Today in some parts of Yunnan province, for example, local people still use traditional tie-dying methods to make different products like scarves and bags.

11
00:01:05,050 --> 00:01:10,210
Tie-dying is not only a form of art but also a lifestyle.
